(PLANTNEST PROJECT SYNOPSIS) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. TITLE OF THE PROJECT) Tj
T* (PlantNest: An Online Plant Store and Community Platform for Plant Lovers) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. INTRODUCTION) Tj
T* (PlantNest is a web-based platform developed to help users discover, purchase, and learn to care for indoor and ornamental plants in a simple and engaging way. The project combines an online plant store, wishlist management, beginner care guidance, order tracking, and a community space where plant lovers can share their experiences and connect with one another. PlantNest is designed to make plant shopping more informative, interactive, and beginner friendly.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. PROBLEM STATEMENT) Tj
T* (Many people want to keep plants at home, but they often face difficulties in selecting suitable plants, understanding care requirements, and finding a reliable platform that offers both products and guidance. Most online shopping platforms focus only on selling plants and do not provide a complete experience that includes beginner support, plant care education, and community interaction. This creates confusion and reduces confidence among first-time buyers.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4. OBJECTIVES) Tj
T* (The main objectives of PlantNest are:) Tj
T* (- To provide an online platform for browsing and purchasing a variety of plants.) Tj
T* (- To allow users to save favorite plants in a wishlist for future purchase.) Tj
T* (- To help users place and track plant orders easily.) Tj
T* (- To guide beginners with simple maintenance tips and plant care suggestions.) Tj
T* (- To create a community page where plant lovers can share their plant journey, experiences, and joy.) Tj
T* (- To deliver a responsive and visually appealing user interface for both desktop and mobile users.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (5. SCOPE OF THE PROJECT) Tj
T* (The scope of PlantNest includes product browsing, filtering, sorting, wishlist management, checkout, order tracking, beginner plant care guidance, and a community feature for user interaction. The project is focused on creating an easy-to-use and attractive experience for plant buyers and enthusiasts. It can be further extended into a larger e-commerce and social platform in future versions.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6. EXISTING SYSTEM) Tj
T* (In the existing system, many online stores only provide product listings and payment options. Users usually have to search other websites or social media pages to understand plant care instructions or to communicate with fellow plant lovers. This separation of shopping, learning, and interaction makes the overall process inconvenient.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (7. PROPOSED SYSTEM) Tj
T* (The proposed system, PlantNest, integrates plant shopping, care guidance, and community interaction into one platform. Users can view plant categories, filter by size, light, and price, sort items as needed, add plants to a wishlist, place orders, and get basic beginner-friendly care guidance. The community feature allows users to share plant updates and connect with others who enjoy growing plants.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8. MODULES OF THE PROJECT) Tj
T* (The major modules of PlantNest are:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8.1 Plant Catalog Module) Tj
T* (Displays a variety of plants with details such as name, category, light requirement, size, price, and description.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8.2 Search, Filter, and Sort Module) Tj
T* (Allows users to search plants by name or category and filter them by size, light requirement, and price range. Sorting options help users browse plants more efficiently.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8.3 Wishlist Module) Tj
T* (Enables users to save favorite plants for future purchase and manage their saved collection.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8.4 Checkout and Order Module) Tj
T* (Allows users to enter delivery details, select payment methods, place orders, and view order history.) Tj
T* () Tj
ET

